{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an arc "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" for each source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p → j"},{"type":"text","text":" for each target "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"j"},{"type":"text","text":". A vertex on both sides of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the 2-cycle"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p → i"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Positions ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< P_s","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index order and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within one in ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"P_s + q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is target incidence ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in the same order. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, and of "},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not offer "},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift#L41"},"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs26DirectedI